# Fix "Module not found: Can't resolve 'recharts'" when running frontend in Docker

The frontend container uses a volume for node_modules. After adding recharts to package.json,
that volume still has the old node_modules. Use one of these:

## Option A – Install inside the running container (quick)

If the frontend container is already running:

  docker compose exec frontend npm install

Then restart the dev server (e.g. stop with Ctrl+C and run `docker compose up` again),
or refresh the app if it hot-reloads.

## Option B – Rebuild the frontend image and recreate the container

From the project root (tradecore/):

  docker compose build frontend --no-cache
  docker compose up -d --force-recreate frontend

This rebuilds the image with recharts and recreates the container (and its node_modules volume).
